invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64.c
catches: rsa_equiv_test
reason: neg_inverse stops Newton's iteration after five steps, the count
  rsa_mont.c's 32-bit limb takes, so the inverse of a 64-bit limb is
  right in its low 32 bits alone. A round of the multiplication then
  leaves a low limb that is not zero and drops it. bin/rsa_equiv_test
  compares the bytes with the 32-bit arm's.

--- old
    for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
        x *= 2U - m0 * x;
--- new
    for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
        x *= 2U - m0 * x;
